<details><summary>Reveal the probability-to-magnetization argument</summary>
If the probability $p$ of a minus spin is bounded by $C<1/2$, then its expectation is $(1-p)-p=1-2p>0$. Establishing $p\le C$ for an actual lattice additionally requires a geometric contour construction.
