<details><summary>Scope and open mathematical steps</summary>
The self-dual identity exactly characterizes a distinguished positive parameter, but identifying it as the unique thermodynamic singularity requires infinite-volume free-energy analysis. The contour majorant is exact, but applying it to Gibbs probabilities requires the contour injection and boundary-condition argument.
